     * Documented: Preserve minutes versus seconds: lookback_time is seconds, lookback_period_min is minutes, and
     * brute-force periods have explicit minute/second names. mark_as_brute describes a two-week block while the
     * excessive-brute command description refers to a one-day block; these pinned descriptions are retained without
     * reconciling their durations.
     *
     * Documented: ipBasedProtection=false precludes firewall-block and IP-period settings per source.
     * can_temp_ban_firewall=0 also makes those capabilities unavailable. The optional nullable warning and conditional
     * restart_ssh remain distinct from omission; no restart behavior is inferred from an absent field.
     *
     * API-map identity: whm1:save_cphulk_config#GET (wire name save_cphulk_config; Settings).
     *
     * @param bool|null $blockBruteForceWithFirewall Whether to use the server firewall to block brute force attacks.
     *     Null omits it.
     * @param bool|null $blockExcessiveBruteForceWithFirewall Whether to use the server firewall to block excessive
     *     brute force attacks. Null omits it.
     * @param int|null $bruteForcePeriodMins The number of minutes over which cPHulk measures all login attempts to a
     *     specific user's account. Null omits it.
     * @param string|null $commandToRunOnBruteForce The command to run when an IP address triggers brute force
     *     protection. Null omits it.
     * @param string|null $commandToRunOnExcessiveBruteForce The command to run when the system blocks an IP address for
     *     a one day period. Null omits it.
     * @param bool|null $ipBasedProtection Whether to enable IP address-based protection on all requests. Null omits it.
     * @param int|null $ipBruteForcePeriodMins The number of minutes in which cPHulk measures an attacker's login
     *     attempts. Null omits it.
     * @param int|null $lookbackPeriodMin The number of minutes over which cPHulk counts failed logins against a user.
     *     Null omits it.
     * @param int|null $markAsBrute The maximum number of failures from a specific IP address before cPHulk blocks that
     *     address for a two-week period. Null omits it.
     * @param int|null $maxFailures The maximum number of failures that cPHulk allows per account within the defined
     *     time range. Null omits it.
     * @param int|null $maxFailuresByip The maximum number of failures from a specific IP address before cPHulk locks
     *     out that address. Null omits it.
     * @param bool|null $notifyOnBrute Whether cPHulk will send a notification when it detects a brute force attack.
     *     Null omits it.
     * @param bool|null $notifyOnRootLogin Whether cPHulk will send a notification when the `root` user successfully
     *     logs in from an IP address that is not on the whitelist. Null omits it.
     * @param bool|null $notifyOnRootLoginForKnownNetblock Whether cPHulk sends a notification upon successful `root`
     *     login when the IP address is not on the whitelist, but from a known netblock. Null omits it.
     * @param bool|null $skipEnabledCheck Whether to skip checking if cPHulk runs on the server. Null omits it.
     * @param bool|null $usernameBasedProtection Whether to enable username-based protection on all requests. Null omits
     *     it.
     * @param bool|null $usernameBasedProtectionForRoot Whether to allow username-based protection to lock out the
     *     `root` user. Null omits it.
     * @param bool|null $usernameBasedProtectionLocalOrigin Whether to enable username-based protection only on requests
     *     that originate from a local IP address. Null omits it.
     * @return SaveConfigResult
     * @throws ApiException If transport, HTTP, the API envelope outcome, or payload validation fails.
     * @throws PayloadMismatchException If the API envelope reported success but the payload differs from the contract;
     *     the operation may already have changed state; do not retry automatically.
     * @see https://api.docs.cpanel.net/specifications/whm.openapi/settings/cphulk-save_cphulk_config
     */
    public function saveConfig(
