    /**
     * Update login security configuration settings.
     *
     * This function modifies a single cPHulk configuration settings as specified.
     *
     * Documented: Available in cPanel & WHM 70 and later.
     *
     * Documented: Changes server-wide security policy. Command inputs may execute when protection is triggered and may
     * contain secrets; they are sensitive arguments and are sent once as form data.
     *
     * Documented: Preserve minutes versus seconds: lookback_time is seconds, lookback_period_min is minutes, and
     * brute-force periods have explicit minute/second names. mark_as_brute describes a two-week block while the
     * excessive-brute command description refers to a one-day block; these pinned descriptions are retained without
     * reconciling their durations.
     *
     * Documented: The key selects the interpretation of value: integer flags, minutes/seconds, failure counts, command
     * strings or comma-separated country codes. The scalar string|int union is preserved without inventing per-key
     * validation.
     *
     * API-map identity: whm1:set_cphulk_config_key#GET (wire name set_cphulk_config_key; Settings).
     *
     * @param string $key The configuration key for the setting to set/modify.
     * @param string|int $value The new value for the specified key.
